    {
      "index": 4,
      "id": "contribution",
      "heading": "Contribution",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c1_makes_three_main_contributions_first",
          "text": "The paper makes three main contributions. First, it introduces a novel formulation of the unbalanced optimal transport problem that connects the rigorous theory of semi-couplings, which allow mass to vary, with a practical and scalable optimal-transport mapping estimator.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "makes",
            "three",
            "main",
            "contributions",
            "first",
            "introduces",
            "novel",
            "formulation",
            "unbalanced",
            "optimal"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s04_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s04_c2_second_derives_computationally_feasi",
          "text": "Second, it derives a computationally feasible implementation based on dual potentials parameterized by input convex neural networks, together with learned reweighting functions that predict mass changes.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "second",
            "derives",
